.TH MOQ5\-RELAY 1 "2026" "MOQ5 Relay" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
moq5\-relay \- deterministic Media over QUIC relay
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B moq5\-relay
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B moq5\-relay
serves Media over QUIC draft\-16 and draft\-18 from a single listener. Terminal
codes are carried by meaning across that boundary: a code is decoded in the
draft that produced it and re\-encoded for the draft that will read it, and one
with no reviewed meaning in the target falls back to that registry's generic
value rather than borrowing a neighbour's.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Run the relay.
.TP
.B capacity
Validate the configuration and print the capacity ceiling, without starting a
listener.
.TP
.B help \fR[\fICOMMAND\fR]
Print help for the relay or for one command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Relay configuration, JSON. Required by
.B serve
and
.BR capacity .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit 0. Answered from the command line alone: no configuration
is read and no transport is started.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including every help and version request.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was malformed, or the configuration was refused.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
moq5\-relay serve --config relay.json
moq5\-relay capacity --config relay.json
.fi
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Human diagnostics are prefixed
.BR "MOQ5 Relay:" .
Structured rows such as
.B RELAY_RUN_CONFIG_V1
are the stable machine contract; the prose is not.
